# Architecture and UI components

Source of truth: AGENTS.md sections 5 to 7, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/DESIGN.md. This file is a summary.

## Layers

- `lib/screens/` composes widgets and holds screen state. No `http`, no JSON parsing, no large inline-styled layouts, no `_buildCard()` helpers that duplicate a widget.
- `lib/widgets/` holds reusable components, one public widget per file, data and callbacks through the constructor. Widgets do not call services or push routes.
- `lib/services/` holds singleton services over `ApiService`. They parse JSON into models and throw readable exceptions. Every new endpoint gets a `MockDataService` handler.
- `lib/models/` holds null-safe classes with `fromJson` and `toJson`. New fields are optional or defaulted.

## Components

Check `lib/widgets/` and the catalog in docs/DESIGN.md first: `MasterContainer`, `CampusMotionBottomBar`, `TopAppBar`, `SectionHeader`, `AppCard`, `AppButton`, `StatItem`, `ActivityCard`, `EventPreviewCard`, `NewsCard`, `PrivacyPolicyDialog`, `ThemedText`.

From a screenshot: map each element to an existing widget, extract the rest into `lib/widgets/` with a widget test, then compose the screen.

## Tokens

- Colours only from `AppColors` (`lib/constants/colors.dart`). No `Color(0x...)` or `Colors.*` in new code.
- Spacing 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32. Radius: cards 20, buttons 14, chips 8.

## Screens and navigation

- Wrap every top-level screen in `MasterContainer`.
- Register every screen in `AppRoutes` and navigate with `Navigator.pushNamed(context, AppRoutes.<name>)`.
- Main tabs use `CampusMotionBottomBar`: 0 Home, 1 Sport, 2 Social, 3 Profile.

## Async and APIs

- `if (!mounted) return;` after every `await` before using `BuildContext`.
- `.withValues(alpha: ...)`, `SharePlus.instance.share(...)`, `activeThumbColor`.
